# Uptime Kuma mutate

## Gate

Load only when the user authorized Uptime Kuma **and** used an explicit
mutate verb this turn (**delete**, **pause**, **resume**, **create**,
**update**) naming the object(s). Otherwise stay on `uptime-kuma-monitors`.
Always pair with `uptime-kuma-safety` before any mutate call.

No Uptime Kuma MCP discovered — use API/UI only. **Do not invent MCP tool
names.**

## Inventory before mutate

1. Resolve monitor/page/channel ids from list this turn
   (`uptime-kuma-monitors`).
2. Prefer **pause** over **delete** when the user only wants quiet.
3. State planned action + ids in one line; then call.

## Live mutate map

| Action | Approach | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Create monitor | API/UI create | type + target required; explicit **create** |
| Update monitor | update by id | only fields user named |
| Pause / resume | pause/resume by id | prefer over delete |
| Delete monitor | delete by id | explicit **delete** |
| Status page create/update/delete | page endpoints/UI | delete needs explicit verb |
| Notification channel create/update/delete | channel endpoints/UI | never echo webhook secrets |
| Bulk pause | only listed ids | no "pause everything" without list |

Confirm exact calls against the instance version.

## Defaults

- Prefer pause over delete when silence is enough.
- Create: require name + type + target from the user; do not invent targets.
- Bulk: only ids listed this turn.
- State which fields you changed in the receipt.

## Operator receipt (mutate)

- action (create/update/pause/resume/delete)
- id(s) + name
- type + target (no secrets)
- resulting status

